// Title: New Generic Credentials Added Via Cmdkey.EXE
// Sigma ID: b1ec66c6-f4d1-4b5c-96dd-af28ccae7727
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-03 | Modified: 2024-03-05
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.005
// Description: Detects usage of "cmdkey.exe" to add generic credentials. As an example, this can be used before
//   connecting to an RDP session via command line interface.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage for administration purposes
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1021.001/T1021.001.md#t1021001---remote-desktop-protocol
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmdkey_adding_generic_creds.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cmdkey.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "cmdkey.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -g" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /g" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –g" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —g" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―g") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -u" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /u" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –u" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —u" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―u") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -p" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /p" or ProcessCommandLine contains " –p" or ProcessCommandLine contains " —p" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―p")
